not only in business, but in sports. And I was like, well, that hasn't really affected my life until I stopped for just another moment and realized I actually turned down a job offer that I really wanted because of the simple fact that it was in Dallas. And as a Houstonian, that was just so unpalatable to me. So Jay, you found that these days much of our connection to our groups is actually motivated by our animosity toward outside groups. Say more about this idea. Yeah, a core part of identity is a sense of us and them. Not only is there a sense of who we are, but who we are not.

117
01:10:43.000 --> 01:11:27.000
